Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to invoke the **`classfloadhk005_runIt`** helper from the `functions` namespace.  
The call passes the two command‑line arguments you mentioned (`/path/to/classes` and `60`) and a reference to a `PrintStream` named `logStream`.  

```java
import static functions.classfloadhk005_runIt;

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Prepare the arguments that the helper expects.
//    • argv  – a *string representation* of a Java array of strings.
//    • out   – a string representation of the PrintStream instance.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------
String argv = "['/path/to/classes', '60']";   // <-- note the single quotes
String out  = "logStream";                    // <-- the variable name of your PrintStream

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Call the helper.  The helper will load the class, invoke the
//    instrumented method, and write diagnostic information to
//    the supplied PrintStream.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------
Object result = classfloadhk005_runIt(new Object[]{argv, out});

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Inspect the result (if any).  The helper typically returns
//    a status string or null.  You can cast it to String if you
